# This crate is used as a named build context by consumers that build it from
# source (`COPY --from=netconf . ./netconf`). Docker reads the ignore file from
# the context directory itself, so without this file the whole of `target/` is
# sent to the builder on every build.
#
# That is not theoretical: on 2026-09-21 a sibling crate's `target/` had grown to
# 16 GB, the contexts together came to roughly 19 GB, and the build died with
# «no space left on device» after filling the daemon's disk.
target/
.git/
